# Commit After OPSX Commands

After `/opsx:apply` or `/opsx:archive` completes successfully, **always commit all changes** before ending the turn.

## When to commit

- After all tasks in `/opsx:apply` are implemented (or the session is paused with completed work)
- After `/opsx:archive` moves the change to the archive directory
- After `/archive-finish` completes its retrospective, verify, and archive steps

## How to commit

1. Stage all related changes (`git add`)
2. Write a concise, imperative commit message summarizing the work
3. Run `git commit`
4. Confirm the commit succeeded with `git status`

## Commit message format

```
# After apply
opsx: implement <change-name> tasks (N/M complete)

# After archive (all tasks done)
opsx: complete and archive <change-name>

# After archive (partial)
opsx: archive <change-name> (with warnings)
```

## Do not skip

- Even if only task checkboxes changed, commit
- Even if the archive only moved a directory, commit
- If pre-commit hooks fail, fix the issue and retry — do not leave uncommitted work
